From 294ca6d89f26329076c949b086c976ad0f5a61ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xie Fei <fei.cn.xie@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:00:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(kv_transfer): publish per-group remote block sizes
 for hybrid KV transfer

EngineCore rewrites `cache_config.block_size` to the minimum of all KV cache
group block sizes, so a DeepSeek-V4 deployment reports 8 even though its
attention groups use 128/512/16384-token pages. The scheduler published that
single scalar as `remote_block_size` for every group, and the decode worker
derived `kernel_size` from its own (128-token) attention group, so the first
KV pull aborted with:

  AssertionError: remote_block_size(8) not divisible by kernel_size(128)

Publish the per-group block sizes alongside the existing scalar and resolve
both sides per KV cache group on the worker. The scalar keeps working for
uniform models and remains the fallback when the new field is absent, so old
peers fail loudly instead of silently pulling misaligned blocks.

A sliding-window group's transfer list is already clipped to its window tail by
the producer, so the decode side must not apply an absolute prompt offset to it
again: select the missing suffix from the tail and let the existing tail/local
trim finish the mapping. Non-sliding groups keep the previous absolute
prefix-skip behavior.

Add regression coverage for the reported six-group geometry, a transfer group
whose index differs from its manager group, the sliding-window prefix tail, and
the unchanged compressed-prefix path.

Signed-off-by: Xie Fei <fei.cn.xie@gmail.com>
